content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-108 – AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-23110, raw-water transfer line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft seal leakage of about one drop every two seconds. The manual treats any leakage at the shaft seal as a fault, with mechanical seal replacement (5.2) and an alignment check (5.4) as the corrective action. No numeric leak-rate limit is given, so plan a repair rather than an immediate stop.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration of 3.2 mm/s falls in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation') of manual Figure 3. It is above Zone A (new machines, up to 2.8) and below Zone C (4.5–7.1, plan maintenance) and Zone D (above 7.1, stop the pump). The site rule to stop immediately applies only in the highest zone (D), so it is not triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature of 68 C is within the manual's 'normal up to 70 C' band. It is 2 C below the top of normal, 12 C below the 80 C alarm and 22 C below the 90 C trip. The site rule requiring a P1 work order applies only above the alarm limit, so it is not triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Serial HF3-23110 is HF3-22000 or above, so Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 applies to this pump for seal part number, gland torque and sleeve acceptance.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked seal faces. This is the most likely cause, especially if the original component seal HF3-450 is still fitted. SB-2026-014 reports early failure of HF3-450 on pumps from serial HF3-22000 because of a revised sleeve tolerance.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment, which is listed as a cause of seal leakage, high vibration and high bearing temperature. It is consistent with vibration in Zone B and a drive-end temperature near the top of the normal band.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal run dry, for example through loss of the Plan 11 flush from pump discharge.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear is a lower-probability contributor to the elevated vibration and temperature. Confirm it by inspection during the repair.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before shutdown, record vibration on both bearing housings (mm/s RMS) and classify the highest reading per Figure 3. Confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from discharge is working, and never run the seal dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Schedule a planned shutdown. Apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit. Drain and vent the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Put a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment in place for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly. Remove the back pull-out assembly; the casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15",
        "C01",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller, then withdraw the seal and shaft sleeve. Record which seal is fitted (HF3-450 or HF3-450B) and the condition of the seal faces.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect shaft sleeve HF3-455 for scoring. Replace it if scoring depth exceeds 0.1 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "While the assembly is out, inspect the bearings and impeller and check grease quantity. If either bearing shows wear or noise, replace both as a pair (HF3-512 drive-end 6312-C3 and HF3-510 non-drive-end 6310-C3).",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit the new cartridge seal HF3-450B. Do NOT fit HF3-450. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed. Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tighten fasteners with lightly oiled threads: seal gland nuts (M10) 30 Nm per SB-2026-014, impeller nut (M24) 160 Nm, casing bolts (M16) 210 Nm, and bearing housing bolts (M12) 85 Nm if disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-align the shaft after reinstalling the assembly. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove isolations and return to service with the seal flush established before starting. Check for seal leakage, and record post-repair vibration on both housings and the bearing housing temperatures against Figure 3 and the 70/80/90 C limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, pre-set (supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (replace whenever casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve – contingency, fit only if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical isolation of the suction and discharge valves.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Line-break permit; drain and vent before opening.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, above the 25 kg site threshold. A lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment are required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the seal dry; confirm the Plan 11 flush on restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration reaches Zone D (above 7.1 mm/s RMS) before the repair, stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. If bearing temperature exceeds the 80 C alarm, escalate to a P1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Contingency – bearing replacement (pair) if wear is found: 6.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts list specifies component seal HF3-450, while SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes it with cartridge seal HF3-450B for serial HF3-22000 and above. P-108 is serial HF3-23110, so the bulletin applies: fit HF3-450B, not HF3-450.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Manual Table 5 gives a seal gland nut torque of 25 Nm, while SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because serial HF3-23110 is in the bulletin's range, 30 Nm applies. All other Table 5 torques remain valid.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Manual 5.2 says only to inspect the sleeve for scoring, whereas SB-2026-014 sets a replacement criterion of more than 0.1 mm scoring depth and removes the need for sleeve measurement with the pre-set HF3-450B. The bulletin criterion applies to this serial.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Which seal is currently installed (original HF3-450 or HF3-450B)? This affects how likely the bulletin failure mode is to be the root cause.",
    "On which bearing housing was the 3.2 mm/s measured, and was it RMS velocity as Figure 3 requires? The non-drive-end reading and the non-drive-end temperature are not reported.",
    "What is the vibration and temperature trend history? 68 C is close to the 70 C normal limit, but there is no baseline.",
    "Is the raw-water line chemically dosed? If so, chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are also required.",
    "Table 6 labour times may be based on the original component seal; the time for the cartridge HF3-450B is not stated.",
    "The manual revision date relative to the bulletin is not given, and it is not stated whether any later bulletin supersedes SB-2026-014.",
    "Does the back pull-out removal disturb motor or bearing housing position? Alignment is planned regardless, as it is also a listed corrective action for seal leakage.",
    "No numeric acceptable seal leakage rate is documented, so the urgency of the drip cannot be quantified against a limit.",
    "The documents give no grease type or quantity, and no NPSH data for the cavitation check."
  ]
}
